  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting competitiveness and income generation in poverty alleviation of small producers in Huancaquito Bajo - El Carmelo Vir - La Libertad</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Centro de Investigacin y Promocin Social &quot;Sara Lafosse&quot; (CIPS &quot;Sara Lafosse&quot;) in cooperation with associations of dairy farmers and fishers and by training new entrepreneurs, CIPS expects to increase the incomes of 200 families in the communities of Huanquito Bajo and El Carmelo, in the district of Vir, La Libertad. It will also promote cooperation among the 22 public and private entities in the Association for the Joint Discussion of Local Development of the Coastal River Basins of the Libertad Region (AMEDIVAC), which will actively support the project. CIPS will use additional funds to incorporate new members, services and activities into the project and further strengthen the capacity of the associations of dairy farmers, artisanal fishers and promoters of community ecotourism to produce and market their products.</narrative>
  </description>
